Depends: ${misc:Depends}, docker.io | docker-ce, systemd, adduser, passwd, ca-certificates, nvidia-container-toolkit | nvidia-container-runtime
Description: LMRS container runner with bundled vLLM and LMCache
 Installs and configures the LMRS Docker container on the host. The package
 pulls or loads the vasilyvz/lmrs image, whose tag equals the release version
 of this package, and creates the container with --gpus all and an explicit
 --shm-size, which vLLM requires for its worker shared memory.
 .
 The image is inference-complete: it carries the LMRS server, pinned vLLM and
 LMCache, and the adapter framework, so no component is installed at run time.
 Nothing is configured inside the image. The host supplies the whole
 configuration surface through mounted volumes: /etc/lmrs with config.json and
 lmcache.yaml, persistent storage for the model disk cache and for LMCache
 runtime artifacts, plus certificates and logs.
 .
 The package creates lmrsuser:lmrsgrp, installs a systemd service unit that
 owns the container lifecycle, and applies the standard network settings so the
 advertised server URL matches what the MCP proxy registers.
 .
 The package version is carried by debian/changelog, the Debian-standard place
 for it, and the release pipeline keeps it equal to the server version, the
 client version and the image tag.
